%S A397673 15,65,136,175,369,444,580,671,1040,1105,1484,1695,2020,2145,2465,
%T A397673 3060,3439,3471,3480,3504,4641,5500,5516,6095,6305,6540,7599,7825,
%U A397673 8224,8996,9855,10545,11700,12056,12209,13345,13740,14911,16040,17220,17985,18335,18561,19240,19924,20111,21340,21455,23775,24465
%N A397673 Shortest sides, r, of right-angled triangles (r,s,x+y) that can be dissected into two distinct integer-sided right-angled triangles corresponding to primitive solutions of five side lengths (r,s,x,y,z).
%C A397673 If there is more than one right-angled triangle for a given r then the value is included more than once. For each right-angled triangle there can be at most one dissection.
%C A397673 A dissection is primitive if the five parameters of the ordered quintuple (r,s,x,y,z) have greatest common divisor 1, where r,s,x,y,z are positive integers such that (x+y)^2 = r^2 + s^2, r^2 = x^2 +z^2, s^2 = y^2 + z^2 and r < s.
%H A397673 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A397673/b397673.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%H A397673 Janaka Rodrigo, <a href="/A397673/a397673_3.txt">Python code for A397673</a>
%e A397673 Let the side lengths of the triangle be r,s,x+y, r<s, with x+y as the hypotenuse, and let the length of the altitude to the hypotenuse be z, which divides the hypotenuse in the ratio x:y.
%e A397673 Positive integer solutions for the ordered quintuple (r,s,x,y,z) start as follows: (15,20,9,16,12), (30,40,18,32,24), (45,60,27,48,36), (60,80,36,64,48), (65,156,25,144,60), ...
%e A397673 The first primitive solution is (15,20,9,16,12), therefore a(1) = 15.
%e A397673 Since the second, third, and fourth solutions are scalar multiples of the first solution, but the fifth solution is primitive.
%e A397673 Therefore, the second term is the value of r in the fifth set, and a(2) = 65.
%o A397673 (PARI) \\ isok will return > 1 if more than one solution, pr flag prints.
%o A397673 isok(r,pr=0)={my(c=0); fordiv(r^2, d, my(s=(r^2/d-d)/2); if(s>r && !frac(s), my(ypx=s+d, x=(ypx-(s^2-r^2)/ypx)/2); if(!frac(x) && issquare(r^2-x^2) && gcd(gcd(r,s),x)==1, c++; if(pr, print([r,s,x,ypx-x,sqrtint(r^2-x^2)])); ))); c}
%o A397673 lista(n,lim=oo)={my(L=List(),k=0); while(#L<n && k<lim, k++; my(c=isok(k)); while(c && #L<lim, c--; listput(L,k))); Vec(L)} \\ _Andrew Howroyd_, Oct 30 2026
